zfswatcher (0.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the web interface with Bootstrap 5.3.9 and htmx 2.0.11 (no
    jQuery); automatic refresh of the dashboard and pool status with the new
    option "refresh" in [www]; the enclosure page is rendered on the server.
    Old Bootstrap 3 CSS class names in the configuration are translated.
  * Add roles for web users (viewer, operator, admin; default admin) and a
    read only JSON API v1 under <rootdir>/api/v1/ with API tokens
    ("zfswatcher -T" creates one).
  * Write internal diagnostics with log/slog to stderr (the journal) and
    add the plug-in interface notifier.Output for output channels.
  * Add a data layer with presentation free model types and snapshots.
  * Remove the unfinished iostat stream; the option "zpooliostatcmd" is
    obsolete and only logs a warning.
  * Log successful configuration reloads at info level.
  * Build the .deb with xz compression, update debian/copyright for the
    bundled assets and raise the CI coverage minimum to 68 %.

 -- tantefred <147740857+tantefred@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100

zfswatcher (0.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Save the pool state to a state file (default
    /var/lib/zfswatcher/state.json, created via StateDirectory=) and report
    only the changes since the last run after a restart.
  * Add a health check at <rootdir>/healthz which needs no login, for
    monitoring tools.
  * Add the option "commandtimeout" for hanging zpool and zfs commands.
  * Add the option "trustedproxies" for X-Forwarded-For and
    X-Forwarded-Proto behind a reverse proxy; log failed web logins as
    warnings with the client address. Document nginx ($http_host) and Caddy
    setups in the README.
  * Shut down the web server gracefully on SIGTERM and SIGINT.
  * Fix parser bugs: a pool without determinable configuration showed a
    bogus device "The"; the iostat stream reader lost entries arriving in a
    single read; a malformed iostat read crashed the daemon.
  * Remove etc/gccgo-build.sh, point the homepage and the RPM spec to the
    maintained fork and relax the Go version check in the RPM spec.
  * Add parser tests with real output of degraded pools and data corruption
    (scenario F).

 -- tantefred <147740857+tantefred@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100

zfswatcher (0.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Harden the web interface: server timeouts and header size limit,
    security headers (CSP, X-Frame-Options, nosniff, Referrer-Policy, HSTS
    with TLS), cross-origin (CSRF) check, locate only via POST with device
    validation and internal redirects only.
  * Store web passwords as bcrypt hashes: "zfswatcher -P" reads the password
    without echo and prints a bcrypt hash. MD5 crypt hashes still work but
    log a deprecation warning at startup. Replace the unmaintained
    github.com/abbot/go-http-auth with a built-in Basic authentication.
  * Warn at startup and on the web pages if a web user still has the
    example password "toor".
  * Update the bundled web assets: Bootstrap 3.3.7 to 3.4.1 (fixes several
    XSS issues) and jQuery 3.2.1 to 3.7.1. Remove the dead html5shim script
    (loaded over http) from the page header.
  * Use net/smtp from the standard library instead of the unmaintained
    github.com/snabb/smtp (no license). Add a 30 second timeout, Message-ID,
    MIME and UTF-8 subject headers, and reject line breaks in headers.
  * Create new log files with mode 0640 instead of 0666.
  * Accept the legacy 9 column zfslistcmd/zfslistusagecmd of 0.4.x
    configurations again (usage data and used space warnings were missing
    since 0.5.0); log a one-time warning recommending to update the
    commands.
  * Report errors instead of ignoring them: a pid file which cannot be
    written is logged as an error, failing locate requests are logged.
  * Reject refresh intervals outside 1 to 86400 seconds.
  * Add a man page for zfswatcher-ledctl.
  * Correct debian/copyright for the bundled files (Bootstrap and jQuery
    are MIT licensed).
  * Drop the recursive chown of /var/log/zfswatcher from postinst; systemd
    LogsDirectory= sets the ownership when the service starts.
  * Add lintian overrides for the intentional static binary and the bundled
    web assets.
  * Vet the FreeBSD and Solaris builds in CI; the FreeBSD build compiles
    without cgo using stubs.

 -- tantefred <147740857+tantefred@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

zfswatcher (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New version 0.5.0, first release of the tantefred fork.
  * Build with Go modules instead of GOPATH and the bundled golibs/.
  * Parse the output of current OpenZFS (2.x): "0B" sizes, remove:,
    checkpoint:, expand: and condense: sections, several scan: lines,
    dedup/special/logs/cache/spares vdev classes, dRAID and the file list
    of "zpool status -v".
  * Fix wrong format arguments in the device state change notifications.
  * Add tests with fixtures from Proxmox VE and Debian 13, and a CI pipeline
    with lint, format, race-detector tests and vulnerability checks.
  * Run the daemon as the system user zfswatcher with a systemd unit (adduser,
    LogsDirectory, hardening). The web interface listens on 127.0.0.1:8081
    by default instead of :80; "bind" stays configurable; drop the SysV init script. Install
    zfswatcher-ledctl and its udev rule. Fix the logrotate rule.
  * Build a static binary without cgo on Linux; the cgo C code crashed
    with SIGILL on CPUs without AVX.
  * Kill external commands after 60 seconds so that a hanging zpool does
    not stop the monitoring.
  * Alert on SUSPENDED pools in the sample configuration. Existing
    configuration files need SUSPENDED:alert in poolstatemap.
  * Use debhelper-compat 13 and Standards-Version 4.7.4.

 -- tantefred <147740857+tantefred@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:22:39 +0100

